<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hinduism</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hindu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hinduism is a major religious tradition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-asia">South Asia</a>, encompassing diverse beliefs, practices and scriptures. It shaped kingship and temple building in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer Empire</a> and was central to the identity of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a>. Hindus formed large subject populations in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>.</p></div>
